From d265932502eb0938d8b4b6290c795adb3f10b662 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:08:54 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add blocking training dummy mode with server-side NPC combat
 animations

- CombatStateService: add OnDamageApplied signal, fired from ApplyDamage.
- NPCCombatAnimationService (new): server-side Animator playback for NPCs using
  CombatAnimationConfig: BlockStart -> BlockLoop, Parry/BlockHit/Hit reactions
  that return to the block, cancelled chains on release/death.
- TrainingDummyConfig (new) and TrainingDummyService: dummy modes (Passive,
  Blocking), periodic block cycle through CombatStateService, SetDead and
  animation cleanup on death.
- DebugService / Testui: "Spawn blocking dummy" action and button.
- Framework: register NPCCombatAnimationService; remove duplicate
  CombatService:Init() call that doubled remote handlers and state replication.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLMaP4V7LcPHCrxoi4fJm8
